{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXPPXX16PFDKCXYW6GCCJV5G","title":"Treat generated policy ownership as exact content","decision":"Require canonical bytes for static agent posture files and a constrained generated shape plus SHA-256 content digest for dynamic native-permission imports before replacing or removing reserved paths.","alternatives":[{"option":"Substring marker detection","why_rejected":"operator extensions retain the markers and can be deleted accidentally"}],"scope":["crates/gommage-cli/src/agent.rs"],"commits":["19a12ca8f1ed828c34dffb9d6492c7dce55be3fc"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1784247415846}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXPPXX1S2G34Z90641SWVVB1","title":"Journal agent integration mutations","decision":"Preflight every selected config and reserved policy path, then restore active files byte-for-byte and remove attempt-created backups if a later agent integration write fails.","alternatives":[{"option":"Rely only on adjacent backups","why_rejected":"a failed multi-file install still leaves partially active policy and hook state"}],"scope":["crates/gommage-cli/src/{agent.rs,quickstart.rs,repair.rs}"],"commits":["19a12ca8f1ed828c34dffb9d6492c7dce55be3fc"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1784247415865}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXPPXX2CZ899J8NX5F4VC4A8","title":"Bound daemon reload acknowledgements","decision":"Apply read/write timeouts and a 4 KiB newline-delimited response limit; treat rejection, timeout, malformed, incomplete, and oversized acknowledgements as setup failures.","alternatives":[{"option":"Best-effort unbounded reload","why_rejected":"a reachable stale daemon can hang installation or report success without applying policy"}],"scope":["crates/gommage-cli/src/daemon.rs"],"commits":["19a12ca8f1ed828c34dffb9d6492c7dce55be3fc"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1784247415884}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXPQKJBTN0B3PETFW67RW2M4","title":"Validate daemon executable before quickstart mutation","decision":"Resolve the daemon binary to a canonical regular executable and make an invalid binary block both dry-run readiness and real setup before integration writes.","alternatives":[{"option":"Trust GOMMAGE_DAEMON_BIN and defer failure to the service manager","why_rejected":"This can report setup success while installing a broken service and can fail only after unrelated host configuration changed."}],"scope":["crates/gommage-cli/src/daemon.rs,crates/gommage-cli/src/quickstart_plan.rs"],"commits":["19a12ca8f1ed828c34dffb9d6492c7dce55be3fc"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1784248125818}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXPR2A5JBVTS5K7QN7XWSEH6","title":"Bound daemon connection establishment","decision":"Use Tokio's existing Unix socket runtime with its time feature so connect, write, and read each have an explicit two-second bound.","alternatives":[{"option":"Keep std UnixStream","why_rejected":"connect and bound only I/O after connection::A full socket backlog can block before read/write timeouts are installed, making the documented bounded reload claim false."}],"scope":["Cargo.toml,crates/gommage-cli/src/daemon.rs"],"commits":["19a12ca8f1ed828c34dffb9d6492c7dce55be3fc"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1784248608946}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXPRCJ143ZFM6HC4WHQDR2CV","title":"Journal quickstart before home initialization","decision":"Capture every known file and directory quickstart may create or replace before layout.ensure, including modes, key, stdlib, runtime sidecars, host config, backups, context, and optional service definition; remove newly-created paths on any Err or failed readiness gate.","alternatives":[{"option":"Journal only host config and reserved policy files after stdlib setup","why_rejected":"A late failure can leave a new signing key, default policies, capability maps, modes, and directories while claiming rollback."}],"scope":["crates/gommage-cli/src/quickstart.rs"],"commits":["19a12ca8f1ed828c34dffb9d6492c7dce55be3fc"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1784248944676}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXPSQTSW649A5JE8VG8RP79J","title":"Bind MCP approvals to exact tool and hook context","decision":"Derive MCP Picto scopes from the exact normalized tool capability and bind default MCP approvals to the canonical hook-enriched input, including a domain-separated hash of the host session identifier when present.","alternatives":[{"option":"Keep global mcp.call and mcp.write scopes","why_rejected":"rejected because one tool can consume a Picto approved for another tool"},{"option":"Use exact-input binding without tool-derived scopes","why_rejected":"rejected because it prevents cross-input consumption but preserves misleading global authority domains and weak diagnostics"},{"option":"Treat caller-supplied session IDs as an independent authenticated security boundary","why_rejected":"rejected because same-UID callers can spoof adapter context; session binding is defense-in-depth inside the canonical input domain"}],"scope":["crates/gommage-core/src/{policy,evaluator,approval,picto,toolcall}.rs","crates/gommage-{cli,mcp,daemon,audit}/**/*","policies/15-agent-tools.yaml","crates/gommage-stdlib/policies/15-agent-tools.yaml"],"commits":["19a12ca8f1ed828c34dffb9d6492c7dce55be3fc"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1784250362684}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXPSTP8KKYK7KA0Q2N6QDYRV","title":"Make local reconfiguration a durable serialized transaction","decision":"Serialize mutating install/repair/quickstart/daemon operations with the standard-library file lock, persist a recoverable transaction journal before mutation, replace regular files through same-directory sync-and-rename writes, preserve symlink identity, and commit only after daemon reload or service readiness succeeds.","alternatives":[{"option":"Keep in-memory rollback journals","why_rejected":"rejected because process death and power loss can leave partial configuration with no recovery record"},{"option":"Use preflight plus optimistic rollback without a lock","why_rejected":"rejected because concurrent legitimate agents can restore stale bytes and delete each other's backups"},{"option":"Add a third-party locking crate","why_rejected":"rejected because Rust 1.89+ provides cross-process File::lock and the workspace toolchain already satisfies it"}],"scope":["crates/gommage-cli/src/{util,agent,repair,quickstart,daemon}.rs","crates/gommage-cli/tests/{cli_reload,cli_quickstart,cli_host_cleanup}.rs"],"commits":["19a12ca8f1ed828c34dffb9d6492c7dce55be3fc"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1784250456339}
